@@ -75,6 +77,39 @@ This will end the request with `400 - Bad Request` status code and the following
 > [!IMPORTANT]
 > Error `statusText` should be short (max 512 to 1024 characters) and only include tab, spaces or visible ASCII characters and extended characters (byte value 128–255). Prefer `message` in JSON body for extended message.
 
+## Problem Details (RFC 9457)
+
+Set the `problemDetails` option to respond errors with the [RFC 9457](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9457) format and the `application/problem+json` content type. It is disabled by default.
+
+```js
+const app = new H3({ problemDetails: true });
+
+app.get("/orders/42", () => {
+  throw new HTTPError({
+    status: 422,
+    message: "Invalid order",
+    type: "https://example.com/probs/validation",
+    instance: "/orders/42",
+    data: { field: "email" },
+  });
+});
+```
+
+```json
+{
+  "data": { "field": "email" },
+  "type": "https://example.com/probs/validation",
+  "title": "Unprocessable Content",
+  "status": 422,
+  "detail": "Invalid order",
+  "instance": "/orders/42"
+}
+```
+
+- `type` defaults to `about:blank`, `title` is `statusText` or the standard phrase of the status, and `instance` is omitted when not set.
+- `data` and `body` are kept as extension members, but the standard members (`type`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`) always win over `body`.
+- [Unhandled errors](#unhandled-errors) ignore `type`, `instance` and `statusText`, and never expose their message.
+
 ## Unhandled Errors
 
 Any error that occurs during calling [request lifecycle](/guide/basics/lifecycle) without using `HTTPError` will be processed as an _unhandled_ error.
